From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:27:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: The debug print level of runtime drivers from
 the PCD

DebugPrintErrorLevelLibHob looks for gEdkiiDebugPrintErrorLevelGuid in
the HOB list at the first DEBUG() of a module, and keeps what it finds.
A runtime driver can print for the first time after ExitBootServices():
ResetSystemRuntimeDxe does in ResetSystem() ("DXE ResetSystem2:
ResetType %s"), and walks the HOB list there, boot services memory,
which macOS and Windows do not map for the runtime services. A build
with DEBUG() then faults in ResetSystem() under them.

Where DEBUG() is built in (DEBUG and NOOPT, and RELEASE with
USE_CBMEM_FOR_CONSOLE, which does not define MDEPKG_NDEBUG), runtime
drivers take BaseDebugPrintErrorLevelLib, which reads
PcdDebugPrintErrorLevel. With coreboot as the boot loader no HOB has
the level, so it stays the same; a universal payload boot loader that
passes one keeps it for every module but the runtime drivers. A RELEASE
build without CBMEM logging has no DEBUG() and does not change.

TEST=A DEBUG payload in a q35 ROM, booting tools/efi/rt-reloc-test.c of
ouroBIOS, which moves the runtime services code and data and calls the
services as boot.efi of macOS does without OpenCore's
AvoidRuntimeDefrag: every service answers and ResetSystem() resets,
where the CPU triple-faulted in GetFirstGuidHob(), reached from the
first DEBUG() of ResetSystemRuntimeDxe. The runtime drivers print the
same messages at boot. The RELEASE payload of the W541 (nri) builds
byte-identical.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc
index b4f6dd1..c6a536d 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc
@@ -688,6 +688,18 @@
   BaseCryptLib|CryptoPkg/Library/BaseCryptLib/RuntimeCryptLib.inf
 !endif
   PcdLib|MdePkg/Library/DxePcdLib/DxePcdLib.inf
+  #
+  # Not DebugPrintErrorLevelLibHob where DEBUG() is built in: a runtime driver
+  # can print for the first time after ExitBootServices(), as ResetSystemRuntimeDxe
+  # does in ResetSystem(), and that library looks for the level in the HOB list
+  # then, boot services memory that macOS and Windows do not map for the runtime
+  # services. With coreboot no HOB has the level: it is PcdDebugPrintErrorLevel
+  # either way. A release build without CBMEM logging has no DEBUG() (MDEPKG_NDEBUG
+  # above) and stays as it is.
+  #
+!if $(TARGET) != RELEASE || $(USE_CBMEM_FOR_CONSOLE) == TRUE
+  DebugPrintErrorLevelLib|MdePkg/Library/BaseDebugPrintErrorLevelLib/BaseDebugPrintErrorLevelLib.inf
+!endif
   MemoryAllocationLib|MdePkg/Library/UefiMemoryAllocationLib/UefiMemoryAllocationLib.inf
   ReportStatusCodeLib|MdeModulePkg/Library/RuntimeDxeReportStatusCodeLib/RuntimeDxeReportStatusCodeLib.inf
   VariablePolicyLib|MdeModulePkg/Library/VariablePolicyLib/VariablePolicyLibRuntimeDxe.inf
